From: leopard-webkit-build
Subject: [PATCH] PlatformMac: add platform/graphics/texmap to WebCore include path

With USE_GSTREAMER_GL now genuinely on (patches 21+22), VideoTextureCopierGStreamer.h
gets compiled. It does `#include "TextureMapperGLHeaders.h"` (quoted, not angle-bracket),
which on non-Mac platforms resolves via the ForwardingHeaders mechanism that
platform/TextureMapper.cmake populates (line 19-36 lists TextureMapperGLHeaders.h
in WebCore_PRIVATE_FRAMEWORK_HEADERS).

PlatformMac.cmake does NOT include(platform/TextureMapper.cmake) — Mac doesn't use
the upstream TextureMapper compositor (Mac uses CALayer directly). So none of the
texmap/ headers are forwarded into WebCore's ForwardingHeaders dir, and the quoted
include fails:

  VideoTextureCopierGStreamer.h:26:10: fatal error: 'TextureMapperGLHeaders.h' file not found

The minimal mechanical fix: add the texmap source directory to WebCore_PRIVATE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES
on Mac. Quoted includes then resolve directly against the source tree. This matches
the existing pattern at PlatformMac.cmake:95-138 which already lists 30+ platform/
subdirectories.

Larger question (out of scope for this patch): the gstreamer GL code path assumes
a TextureMapper-based compositor. On Mac, bridging GstGLMemory to CAOpenGLLayer
either requires adopting TextureMapper on Mac (significant platform change) or
writing a Cocoa-specific compositor bridge (the multi-day consumer port scoped
in spikes/gstreamer-gl-investigation/). Either is multi-session work; this patch
just unblocks the compile.

---
diff --git a/Source/WebCore/PlatformMac.cmake b/Source/WebCore/PlatformMac.cmake
--- a/Source/WebCore/PlatformMac.cmake
+++ b/Source/WebCore/PlatformMac.cmake
@@ -132,6 +132,7 @@ list(APPEND WebCore_PRIVATE_INCLUDE_DIRECTORIES
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/graphics/opentype"
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/graphics/opengl"
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/graphics/mac"
+    "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/graphics/texmap"
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/mac"
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/mediacapabilities"
     "${WEBCORE_DIR}/platform/mediarecorder/cocoa"
